            <ArticleTitle>Anticoagulant and platelet-antiaggregating therapy in stroke and threatened stroke.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>223-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author presents studies suggesting that anticoagulants are not indicated in completed stroke except when it is caused by an embolus from a well-defined cardiac source. Preferred and alternate treatment and therapy for stroke and threatened stroke is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
